{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>And you returned and wept, etc. And HaShem did not hear, etc.</b> One needs to know the intent of the verse: if the intention here is that they returned from the battle and wept over those whom the Amorites had struck of them, the narrative on this is not clearly known. Also His saying <b>and He did not hear</b> etc. <b>and He did not listen</b> etc. — if the weeping was over a misfortune that had befallen them, what place is there for this statement? Rather, it appears that the intent of the verse is that after the Amorites struck them, they submitted themselves before HaShem and returned in repentance, also with weeping over sin, according to the manner of those who return; and even so, their stench had grown so great that HaShem did not hear their repentance and did not listen to their weeping."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:27.100967051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}